# Build context for the Dockerfile.
#
# The image installs its own dependencies in the deps stage and then runs
# `COPY . .`. Without this file that COPY lands on top of the freshly installed
# node_modules with whatever happens to be sitting in the checkout — and the
# deploy does `git reset --hard`, which leaves untracked directories in place.
# A stale node_modules or .next on the runner would silently replace the one
# the image just built, and the failure would look like a code bug.

# Dependency and build output, at every level
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist

# Secrets. Not in the runner's checkout because they are gitignored, but a
# local `docker build` would otherwise bake them into an image layer, where
# they survive deletion.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# The Android project. Nothing in the web build imports it, and it is 77 files
# of Gradle scaffolding that would be copied on every deploy.
android_app

# Version control and editor state
.git
.github
.claude
*.log

# Documents — several megabytes of PDF and DOCX with no role in the image
docs
